IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g7-regulations`
IMPORT `g8-fees-nouns`
IMPORT `g8-fees`

-- int-fees.l4: headline (e), the fee for a service in a vintage, and the mapping between the two ways the fleet counts what s.59 lets
-- the Minister charge for.  The INTEGRATOR's module.
--
-- Three counts of the same thing.  The PLAN (section (b), G8) counted FIVE heads of fee in s.59; group 7 (fork F-R-1) enumerates SIX
-- (one per "for" phrase: the application; the grant or renewal; the examinations with objections; the s.17 training; and, at a
-- different rate for a foreign expert's temporary licence, the application or renewal and, separately, the grant); group 8 prices NINE
-- services (the exam head split into the practical and theoretical sitting and the objection to each).  They do not conflict: the
-- nine services fall under the six heads.  The mapping below makes that checkable, and the tests assert it for every vintage: a
-- vintage that is silent on every service under a head is silent on the head, which is what group 7 told group 8 to do (trap T38).

§ `Headline (e): the fee for a service in a vintage, and s.59's heads of fee`

§§ `Which head of s.59 a service falls under`

@ref Law s.59; Fees Regulations regulations 1 and 2
@desc The head of fee under s.59 (group 7's enumeration) that a service group 8 prices falls under
GIVEN service IS A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
GIVETH A `Head of fee under section 59`
`int — the head of fee under section 59 for the service` service MEANS
    CONSIDER service
    WHEN `the service of filing an application for a licence or its renewal` THEN `a fee for submitting an application for a licence`
    WHEN `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal` THEN `a fee for the grant of a licence, or for its renewal`
    WHEN `the service of filing an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal` THEN `a different rate of fee for submitting an application for a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or for its renewal`
    WHEN `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` THEN `a different rate of fee for the grant of a temporary licence for a foreign expert`
    WHEN `the service of sitting a practical exam` THEN `a fee for the examinations required for a final certificate, including an objection to an examination`
    WHEN `the service of sitting a theoretical exam` THEN `a fee for the examinations required for a final certificate, including an objection to an examination`
    WHEN `the service of objecting to the score of a practical exam` THEN `a fee for the examinations required for a final certificate, including an objection to an examination`
    WHEN `the service of objecting to the score of a theoretical exam` THEN `a fee for the examinations required for a final certificate, including an objection to an examination`
    WHEN `the service of attending a continuing training course` THEN `a fee for the continuing training under section 17`

@ref Law s.59
@desc Every service group 8 prices
GIVETH A LIST OF `Service under the Fees Regulations`
`int — every service under the Fees Regulations` MEANS
    LIST
        `the service of filing an application for a licence or its renewal`,
        `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal`,
        `the service of filing an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal`,
        `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence`,
        `the service of sitting a practical exam`,
        `the service of sitting a theoretical exam`,
        `the service of objecting to the score of a practical exam`,
        `the service of objecting to the score of a theoretical exam`,
        `the service of attending a continuing training course`

@ref Law s.59
@desc The services group 8 prices that fall under the head
GIVEN head IS A `Head of fee under section 59`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Service under the Fees Regulations`
`int — the services that fall under the head` head MEANS
    filter (GIVEN service YIELD `int — the head of fee under section 59 for the service` service EQUALS head) `int — every service under the Fees Regulations`

@ref Law s.59, Fees Regulations (trap T38)
@desc True if the vintage prints a figure for at least one service under the head; false if it is silent on every one of them (a vintage silent on a head answers silence)
GIVEN vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
      head IS A `Head of fee under section 59`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`int — the vintage prices the head` vintage head MEANS
    any (GIVEN service YIELD isJust (`the amount the Fees Regulations state in` vintage `for the service` service)) (`int — the services that fall under the head` head)

@ref Law s.59
@desc The heads of fee of s.59 that the vintage prints a figure for
GIVEN vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Head of fee under section 59`
`int — the heads of fee the vintage prices` vintage MEANS
    filter (GIVEN head YIELD `int — the vintage prices the head` vintage head) (`s 59 — the heads of fee for which the Minister may set a fee`)

§§ `Headline (e): the fee`

@ref Law s.59; Fees Regulations regulations 2 and 3; regulation 5 and the amendment of 2026
@export The fee for a service in a vintage of the Fees Regulations on a day: the figure the vintage prints, updated by regulation 3 from the first 1 January after the regulations came into force by the readings of the index; nothing where the vintage is silent on the service (never a figure from another vintage) or the text was not yet in force; a named refusal where an update needs a reading that was not supplied or the vintage is the draft, which was never in force
GIVEN vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations` @desc Which text: the SimpLEX draft (never in force), the regulations as made (9 July 2025) or as amended (4 May 2026)
      service IS A `Service under the Fees Regulations` @desc What is charged for
      day IS A DATE @desc The day for which the fee is asked (the sources do not say whether the day of application, payment or service)
      readings IS A LIST OF `Price index reading` @desc The consumer price index readings with their publication days; the sources give none
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`int — the fee in the vintage for the service on the day` vintage service day readings MEANS
    `the fee under the Fees Regulations in the vintage for the service on the day` vintage service day readings

@ref Law s.59; Fees Regulations regulations 2 and 3
@export The vintage of the Fees Regulations in force on a day, if any: none before 16.7.2025, the text as made to 3.5.2026, as amended from 4.5.2026
GIVEN day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about
GIVETH A MAYBE `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
`int — the vintage of the Fees Regulations in force on the day` day MEANS
    `the vintage of the Fees Regulations in force on` day
